Along the lines of the #appraise suggestion, maybe there could be some sort
of item, say a spellbook of prices or a price marker (?) that could be used to
give the approximate prices. You would learn the spellbook like a normal spell
and it would work like a poor man's identify. The marker would have limited
charges and each time it is used it would leave a small sticky label with the
the price on, on the item. If it is cursed you'll get the wrong price, if it
is blessed you'll get the exact price.

If rope becomes a Nethack item, a possible use for it would be to tie it to
objects and drag them along behind you, in a similar way to how a chain and
ball is dragged. This would mean you could drag chests, boulders, bodies etc.
However dragging would be noisy, slow and limiting to your attack bonuses, and
if you were to drag an item over a trapdoor or some stairs it would drag you
down.

I haven't been able to play nethack 3.07 yet, but has the bug where monsters
can accurately throw weapons at you when you are invisible been fixed ?


